      "standardized_narrative": "At the 2017 year end the Syndicate's opening gross claims reserves were GBP 1,103.3m. The Syndicate recorded a net release from prior year reserves of GBP 59.2m, driven primarily by more favourable claims development and efficient claims handling. Partially offsetting this was a GBP 52.4m strengthening due to the February 2017 Ogden discount rate change which adversely impacted reserves on 2014 and prior UK Motor treaty business. The 2017 underwriting result was also materially impacted by GBP 74.7m of natural catastrophe losses in Q3/Q4 2017 (Harvey, Irma, Maria, Mexico City earthquake, Northern California wildfires, Nate, Southern California wildfires). RITC activity (acceptance from Syndicate 1400) has restated historical development tables and may distort development patterns.",
